[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Intake and pipeline low-level requirements
UID: FMD-LLR-INT
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Low-level requirements of the intake and pipeline item, written from the code as built:
`flightmd_core/services/format_detector.py`, `flightmd_core/services/compressed.py`,
`flightmd_core/services/columns.py`, `flightmd_core/cache.py`, `flightmd_core/orchestrator.py`,
`flightmd_core/__main__.py` and `flightmd_core/__init__.py`. Parents are in `hlr-int.sdoc`. The design is in
`docs/lifecycle/06-design/lld-int.md`. Where a statement says "as built" the behaviour is recorded as found and
is listed as a gap in section 6 of the design.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Format detection (flightmd_core/services/format_detector.py)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ULog magic
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format_from_header` returns `"px4_ulog"` when the first 7 bytes are `ULog\x01\x12\x35`, before any
other check and whatever the file name.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Binary dataflash head
STATEMENT: >>>
`_check_dataflash` returns `True` when bytes 0 and 1 are `0xA3 0x95`, byte 2 is `0x80` (the FMT message type)
and every byte present at offsets 5 to 8 (the FMT name) is 0, an ASCII digit or an ASCII upper-case letter;
offsets past the end of the buffer count as valid. `detect_format_from_header` then returns `"ardupilot_bin"`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blackbox marker
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format_from_header` returns `"betaflight_bbl"` when `looks_like_blackbox` finds the blackbox start line
anywhere in the header; this check comes third, after ULog and binary dataflash.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Text dataflash first line
STATEMENT: >>>
`_check_text_dataflash` returns `False` when the buffer holds a zero byte; otherwise it removes one leading
UTF-8 byte order mark and leading carriage returns, line feeds, tabs and spaces and returns `True` when the rest
starts with `FMT,` followed by two integers, two words and one more word character, comma separated with at most
one space after each comma. `detect_format_from_header` then returns `"ardupilot_log"`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI .DAT is recognised and refused
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format_from_header` raises `UnsupportedFormatError` with the message `DAT_UNSUPPORTED` and
`format_id="dji_dat"` when `looks_like_dji_dat` is true for the header (`BUILD` at offset 16, or `LOGH` at
offset 0), after the four checks above and before the telemetry-log check.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Length of one telemetry-log record
STATEMENT: >>>
`_tlog_frame_len(buf, pos)` returns -1 when fewer than 9 bytes remain after `pos`, and `None` when the first
byte of the 8-byte big-endian timestamp is not 0 or the byte after the timestamp is neither `0xFE` nor `0xFD`.
For `0xFE` (MAVLink 1) the length is 8 + 6 + payload length + 2. For `0xFD` (MAVLink 2) it returns `None` when
the incompatibility flags have any bit other than `0x01`, else the length is 8 + 10 + payload length + 2, plus
13 when bit `0x01` (signed) is set. It returns -1 when the buffer ends before the length byte, the flags byte or
the end of the record.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Three records in a row make a telemetry log
STATEMENT: >>>
`_check_tlog(buf, complete)` walks records from offset 0 and returns `True` after `TLOG_FRAMES_NEEDED` = 3
valid records, or, when `complete` is true, when the buffer ends exactly after one or two valid records. It
returns `False` at the first position that is not a record and `None` when the buffer ends inside a record.
`detect_format_from_header` returns `"mavlink_tlog"` on `True`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Provisional telemetry log from a short header
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format_from_header` returns `"mavlink_tlog"` when `_check_tlog` returned `None`, `complete` is false,
the file name ends in `.tlog` (case ignored) and the first byte of the header is 0. With any other extension the
same header is refused.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: DJI flight record, sure or provisional
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format_from_header` returns `"dji_txt"` when `check_dji_txt(header, complete)` is true, and also when it
returned `None`, `complete` is false and the file name ends in `.txt` (case ignored). This is the last positive
check.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Refusal messages and the error class
STATEMENT: >>>
`UnsupportedFormatError` is a `ValueError` with an attribute `format_id`, `None` unless given. When no check
matched, `detect_format_from_header` raises it with a message that the `.log` file is not an ArduPilot
text-format dataflash log when the name ends in `.log`, and otherwise with "Unrecognized log format", the file
name in brackets when one was given, and the list of supported formats.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Detection of a file on disk
STATEMENT: >>>
`detect_format(file_path)` reads the first `HEADER_BYTES` = 4096 bytes, sets `complete` to true only when fewer
than 4096 bytes were read, and returns `detect_format_from_header(header, basename, complete)`. As built a file
of 4096 bytes or more is therefore never `complete`, and the provisional rules of LLR-INT-008 and LLR-INT-009
apply to it.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Parser table
STATEMENT: >>>
`PARSERS` maps exactly the identifiers `px4_ulog`, `ardupilot_bin`, `ardupilot_log`, `mavlink_tlog`,
`betaflight_bbl`, `dji_txt` and `dji_dat` to a class with a `parse` method; `dji_txt` and `dji_dat` both map to
`DJIParser`. The module also defines `SUPPORTED_EXTENSIONS` (`.ulg .ulog .bin .tlog .log .bbl .bfl .txt`),
which detection does not use.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-001

