[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-043
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Progress steps
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` reports these steps: 5 "Reading flight log" with an estimate of size in MB / 4 plus the analysis
estimate (`ANALYSIS_BASE_S` = 2.0 s plus `ANALYSIS_S_PER_MB` = 0.04 s per MB); 5 to 60 during the parse, or 60
"Using the earlier parse of this log" on a cache hit; 62 before the weather lookup (online only); 65 before the
analysers; 80 before scoring; 88 before the explanations; 92 before the AI summary (only when used); 96 before
the report is assembled; 100 "Done." with 0.0 s left. After the parse the time left is the analysis estimate
less the time spent since the parse, never below 0.5 s.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests check that percentages never fall, that the first estimate is positive and that the last call is 100
with 0. The individual step values are checked by review.
<<<
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-044
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Cache use in the pipeline
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` computes `file_sha256(ulog_path)` and, when `cache.enabled()`, calls `cache.get` in the thread
pool; an `OSError` from it is logged and treated as a miss. On a hit it uses the cached
`(topics, params, metadata)` and does not open, detect or parse. On a miss it calls `_open_and_parse`, sets
`metadata.log_sha256`, and when the cache is on calls `cache.put` at once, before armed windows, path, weather
or place name are added; an `OSError` from the write is logged and ignored.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-017
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-045
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Return and error contract
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis(ulog_path, file_name, file_size, progress_callback=None, ai_enhancer=None)` must be awaited on a
running event loop and returns the `FlightMDReport` made by `ReportBuilder().build` from the results, the
explained findings, the metadata, the score triple, the summary, `file_name`, `file_size` and the start time in
milliseconds; `file_name` and `file_size` are passed on as given. The errors it raises for an unusable log are
`ValueError`. As built nothing after the parse is wrapped, so an exception from the later steps leaves with its
own type.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-012
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-017

