[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-047
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Armed windows
STATEMENT: >>>
`_armed_windows(topics, end_s)` returns `None` when `vehicle_status` is missing, empty or has no
`arming_state` column. Otherwise it sorts by `timestamp` (microseconds), takes a row as armed when
`arming_state == 2`, starts a window at the time of each row that turns armed and ends it at the time of the row
that turns disarmed, starts one at the first row when that row is armed, and ends an open window at
`max(end_s, last row time)`. Times are seconds rounded to 3 decimals; the result is a list of `[start, end]`,
empty when no row is armed.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-015

