STATEMENT: >>>
`_gps_track` uses `vehicle_gps_position` when it has `lat` and `lon`: it keeps rows where both are not 0 and,
when `fix_type` exists, `fix_type >= 2`, and when any row is left returns a frame sorted by `timestamp` with
`lat` and `lon` divided by 1e7 (degrees), `alt` from `alt` or else `alt_ellipsoid` divided by 1000 (millimetres
to metres; NaN when neither exists) and `hdop` from `hdop` or else `eph` when one exists. As built a row whose
`lat` or `lon` is NaN passes the not-0 test.
