STATEMENT: >>>
When the receiver topic gives no row, `_gps_track` uses `vehicle_global_position` when it has `lat` and `lon`:
it keeps rows where either is not 0 and returns `timestamp`, `lat`, `lon` (already degrees) and `alt` (metres,
NaN when the column is missing), sorted by `timestamp`, with no `hdop`. It returns `None` when neither topic
gives a row.
