[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-051
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Path points
STATEMENT: >>>
`_fill_path` takes every `step`-th row of the track, `step = max(1, len(track) // PATH_POINTS)` with
`PATH_POINTS` = 500, and sets `metadata.gps_path` to `[lat, lon, alt]` with NaN replaced by 0.0,
`metadata.gps_path_t_s` to the row times in seconds rounded to 3 decimals, and, when the track has `hdop`,
`metadata.gps_path_hdop` to the values with `None` for values that are not finite. As built the path holds up
to 999 points (a track of 999 rows gives step 1), and no point is left out for being implausible.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-016

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-052
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Altitude, distance and speed from the track
STATEMENT: >>>
Only where the parser left the field `None`, `_fill_path` sets `max_altitude_m` to the highest finite track
altitude less the first finite one (rounded to 0.1 m), and from the whole track, with an equirectangular
projection on a 6 371 000 m sphere, sets `total_distance_m` to the sum of the plausible segments (rounded to
0.1 m) and `max_speed_ms` to the fastest plausible segment (rounded to 0.01 m/s). A segment is plausible when it
lasts at least `MIN_GPS_DT_S` = 0.05 s and its speed is at most `MAX_PLAUSIBLE_SPEED_MS` = 75 m/s. Segments left
out are not reported anywhere.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: intake
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HLR-INT-016

[REQUIREMENT]
