TITLE: Weather and place name
STATEMENT: >>>
`run_analysis` takes the first track point as the position. With no track it sets `metadata.weather` to
`_no_weather("No GPS position data in log")`; when `offline()` to
`_no_weather("Weather lookup is off (offline mode)")`, with no network call. Otherwise it calls `fetch_weather(lat,
lon, log_start_utc)` when `metadata.log_start_utc` is set, else sets
`_no_weather("Flight date unknown, so no weather lookup")`, and sets `metadata.location_name` from
`reverse_geocode(lat, lon)`. `_no_weather(reason)` is a dict with `temperature_max_c`, `temperature_min_c`,
`wind_speed_max_ms` and `rain_sum_mm` all `None` and `description` the reason.
<<<
