[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LLR-INT-072
STATUS: Active
TITLE: How a result is compared with its golden
STATEMENT: >>>
`test_corpus_log_matches_golden` skips when the golden is missing or the log cannot be downloaded, and fails
when the downloaded file's SHA-256 differs from the manifest. It asserts: detected format equals the manifest;
score within `score_band`; `findings` and `assessed_modules` equal; every metric in the golden present and
within 10 % relative or 0.05 absolute, whichever is wider, unless the golden's `tolerances` block overrides it;
metadata equal, `duration_seconds` within 1.0 s. Not compared: the number, order, confidence, evidence, time
windows and explanations of findings, parameter recommendations, grade and label, the assessed fraction, parse
warnings, armed windows, the path, and metrics that are new.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
This is test code and is not itself under test. A review reads the assertions.
<<<
